<title>AUSTRALIA: Three Australia states face drought-farmers group.</title>
<headline>Three Australia states face drought-farmers group.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-05-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australian farmers in three states face potentially severe drought conditions, the National Farmers' Federation (NFF) said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Ten percent of Queensland, 40 percent of New South Wales and 25 percent of Victoria were facing severe drought, the NFF's executive director Wendy Craik said.</p>
<p>&quot;Even though useful rain has fallen over the last few days, handfeeding of stock, sales of stock and reduced grain crops are the consequences and the the longer term rainfall outlook, with the southern oscillation index at 16.2, is not encouraging,&quot; Craik told the NFF's annual conference in Canberra.  </p>
<p>Western New South Wales and the Monaro region, southeast and southwest Queensland, southwest Gippsland and northern Victoria are the worst hit areas, she said.</p>
<p>-- Sydney newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
